translation:
Unmoving, the One—the Self-reality (ātmatattva)—is swifter than the mind;
the gods, the senses (indriyāṇi), did not reach it: it had gone ahead.
Though itself standing still, it outstrips, as it were, the others as they run;
in it Mātariśvan, the Wind, distributes—or sustains—the activities (karmāṇi).
